Paul Peters: Location Geocoding, Weather API
weather_service.py takes the user's city and optional country code and converts it into latitude and longitude using the Open-Meteo Geocoding API.
The coordinates are then used to retrieve current weather conditions and a three-day forecast from the Open-Meteo Weather API.
weather_service.py organizes the weather data, including temperature, humidity, precipitation, and evapotranspiration, into a structured format that can be used by other modules for watering recommendations.
test_weather.py contains three automated unit tests to verify the weather module's functionality.
The module also handles invalid city inputs by displaying an error message when a location cannot be found.

